/* book Worked example 2: Q: A standard fiber has λ₀ = 1310 nm and S₀ = 0.092 ps/(nm²·km). (a) Find D at 1550 nm. (b) A DFB laser at 1550 nm has a 20 GHz spectral width; convert it to nm and find the spread over 80 km.
   1. (a) λ₀⁴/λ³ = 1310⁴ ÷ 1550³ = 2.945 × 10¹² ÷ 3.724 × 10⁹ = 790.9 nm.
   2. D = (0.092/4)(1550 − 790.9) = 0.023 × 759.1 = 17.5 ps/(nm·km).
   3. (b) Δλ = λ²Δf/c = (1.55 × 10⁻⁶)² × 20 × 10⁹ ÷ (3 × 10⁸) = 2.4025 × 10⁻¹² × 66.67 = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁰ m = 0.160 nm.
   4. Δτ = 17.5 × 80 × 0.160 = 224 ps.
   Answer: D ≈ 17.5 ps/(nm·km); the 20 GHz line is 0.16 nm wide and spreads by about 224 ps over 80 km, more than two bit periods at 10 Gbit/s. */
